      "explanation": "Harris makes rejecting the misery intuition grounds for discounting everything subsequently said, explicitly insulating it through a semantic exclusion. However, he supplies a substantive argument about the meaning of bad at E1645–1680. Peterson accepts the intuition while disputing its factual status (E1682–1691); this is protection within an argument, not an unsupported slogan."
