      "emotionalDevices": ["comfort"],
      "confidence": "medium",
      "explanation": "The guarantee exceeds the reason supplied: sincere reflection can generate corrective insight, but universal success is not established. Accepting any answer and expecting an unwelcome one (E2334–2343) could accommodate contrary experiences. Still, Peterson never explicitly counts silence as success, and his later defense concerns this particular psychological exercise (E2353–2362)."
    },
