      "protection": "yes",
      "emotionalDevices": ["none"],
      "confidence": "high",
      "explanation": "Peterson dismisses the ignorance account by making belief in it evidence of inadequate experience, rather than explaining why encountering malevolence defeats that account. His earlier distinction between suffering and malicious pleasure (E1753–1766) supplies relevant background, but does not earn this dismissal. He subsequently accepts Harris's broader objection about incompatible traditions (E2433–2435)."
    }
